409	  <h2>Where three real defects actually got introduced</h2>
410	  <p class="lede">From this session, not hypotheticals.</p>
411	  <div class="scroller">
412	    <table>
413	      <caption>Lumen — traced back to origin</caption>
414	      <thead>
415	        <tr><th>Defect</th><th>Introduced at</th><th>Would've been caught by</th></tr>
416	      </thead>
417	      <tbody>
418	        <tr>
419	          <td class="defect">ClaudeCodeAdapter defaulted to a real, priced model
420	            <span class="meta">codex.rs already had this exact fix — it never propagated</span>
421	          </td>
422	          <td><span class="tag">vector — plan</span></td>
423	          <td>Plan task for one <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">SessionAdapter</span> impl, not all four</td>
424	        </tr>
425	        <tr>
426	          <td class="defect"><span style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">is_fully_priced</span> hardcoded true on store read-back
427	            <span class="meta">no column existed; field silently defaulted every round-trip</span>
428	          </td>
429	          <td><span class="tag">canon — spec</span></td>
430	          <td>Spec never asked "does this field survive the store crate boundary"</td>
431	        </tr>
432	        <tr>
433	          <td class="defect"><span style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">tool_counts</span> always empty in shipped output
434	            <span class="meta">read path shipped; write path never wired</span>
435	          </td>
436	          <td><span class="tag">canon — spec</span></td>
437	          <td>Same boundary gap — the record type never carried what the read side needed</td>
438	        </tr>
439	      </tbody>
440	    </table>
441	  </div>
442	
443	  <h2>Three insertions</h2>
444	  <p class="lede">Language-agnostic — the mechanism differs per stack, the question doesn't.</p>
445	  <div class="mechanisms">
446	    <div class="mech">
447	      <div class="mech-head"><span class="mech-num">01</span><h3>Interface-completeness check</h3></div>
448	      <p>When a task touches one implementer of a shared trait / interface / protocol, the plan must cover every other implementer, or state explicitly why not.</p>
449	      <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> vector:challenger, as an eighth review dimension. Mechanical, not judgment — enumerate implementers, diff against planned tasks.</div>
450	    </div>
451	    <div class="mech">
452	      <div class="mech-head"><span class="mech-num">02</span><h3>Boundary round-trip check</h3></div>
453	      <p>When a criterion introduces a field on a type another spec persists, serializes, or transmits, that far-side spec needs a matching round-trip criterion — or the gap is named on purpose.</p>
454	      <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> canon:audit-spec, as a sixth audit dimension alongside its current five.</div>
455	    </div>
456	    <div class="mech">
457	      <div class="mech-head"><span class="mech-num">03</span><h3>Default to unrepresentable-by-construction</h3></div>
458	      <p>A value that's sometimes absent, sometimes wrong, or sometimes stale should be a sum type / discriminated union / <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">Result</span> by default — not a bool sitting next to a number, checked by convention. Applies equally to a Rust enum, a TS discriminated union, or a sealed class elsewhere.</p>
459	      <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> lambda:implementer's default posture for boundary-crossing fields — reach for this before <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">canon:architect</span> is escalated to, not after.</div>
460	    </div>
461	  </div>
462	
463	  <h2>Where the human sits</h2>
464	  <p class="lede">Two required pauses — both before a line of implementation code exists.</p>
465	  <div class="protocol">
466	    <div class="step">
467	      <div class="step-icon">01</div>
468	      <div><b>canon</b> drafts + gates a spec<div class="note">research-report and tradeoffs attached, not just the passing criteria</div></div>
469	    </div>
470	    <div class="step gate">
471	      <div class="step-icon">GATE</div>
472	      <div><b>Publish spec + tradeoffs as an artifact</b><div class="note">short comparison table, not prose — sign-off before vector plans anything</div></div>
473	    </div>
474	    <div class="step">
475	      <div class="step-icon">02</div>
476	      <div><b>vector</b> plans + challenges<div class="note">interface-completeness check runs here</div></div>
477	    </div>
478	    <div class="step gate">
479	      <div class="step-icon">GATE</div>
480	      <div><b>Publish plan + task table as an artifact</b><div class="note">sign-off before lambda writes anything</div></div>
481	    </div>
482	    <div class="step">
483	      <div class="step-icon">03</div>
484	      <div><b>lambda → axiom → proof</b> run to completion<div class="note">no further pause — this part was already trustworthy</div></div>
485	    </div>
486	  </div>
487	
488	  <h2>Token discipline</h2>
489	  <div class="discipline">
490	    <div class="rule"><div class="verb">Tables, not paragraphs</div><p>Tradeoffs as a comparison grid. Findings as criterion_id / type / fix rows, matching canon's existing issue format.</p></div>
491	    <div class="rule"><div class="verb">One diagram, not a narrative</div><p>A plan is a task list a human can scan in ten seconds — not a chat transcript reconstructed as prose.</p></div>
492	    <div class="rule"><div class="verb">Flag, don't restate</div><p>Checkpoint artifacts show deltas and open questions — never the full spec text the human already saw.</p></div>
493	  </div>
494	
495	  <footer>
496	    <span class="ask">Pick a starting point:</span> draft the vector:challenger dimension, the canon:audit-spec dimension, or the lambda default-posture instruction — or pilot the two-gate checkpoint manually on the next spec before wiring any of it in.
497	  </footer>
498	</div>
499	
500	<script>
501	  try {
502	    document.getElementById('dateline').textContent = new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10);
503	  } catch (e) {}
504	</script>
